[142.565496, "o", "  qwen3.6-35b — 1 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 1 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n[approval] propose skill \"repairing broken pip in the python:3.13 image\" — approved\r\n  ⚙ skill \r\n    ✓ skill repairing-broken-pip-in-the-python-3-13-image proposed\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\nFixed. Your system pip works again.\r\n\r\n**What was wrong:** the `pip/` package itself was missing from disk. `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/` still had `pip-24.3.1.dist-info/` (metadata, RECORD listing every file) but not the files it described. So `pip`, `pip3` and `python3 -m pip` all died at startup with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'\r\n```\r\n\r\nWorth clearing out of the way: this is *not* PEP 668. The `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` file on this box belongs to Debian's Python 3.11 at `/usr/lib/python3.11/`; you"]
[142.565529, "o", "r `python3` is the official `python:3.13` image at `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no such file. No venv is needed to install system-wide here — the install was root-owned and you are root.\r\n\r\n**The fix:** `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade` does *not* repair this — it sees the surviving dist-info, decides pip is \"already satisfied\", and leaves you broken. The working route was unpacking the bundled wheel over the top:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages\r\npython3 -m zipfile -e /usr/local/lib/python3.13/ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl .\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Verification** (run after the repair, independently of it):\r\n\r\n```\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\nDRY-RUN INSTALL OK\r\nREAL INSTALL OK 1.17.0\r\n```\r\n\r\n`python3 -m pip install --target /tmp/realinstall six` fetched from PyPI, unpacked, and `import six` succeeded — a genuine end-to-end install, done with `--target` so your system site-packages were not touched by the test.\r\n\r\nOne leftover: I"]
[142.565538, "o", " proposed a skill capturing this failure mode and its fix, so it isn't re-derived next time. It's sitting at `.gnomon/skills/proposed/repairing-broken-pip-in-the-python-3-13-image.md` and only becomes active if you run `gnomon skill accept repairing-broken-pip-in-the-python-3-13-image` — accepting changes the surface hash, which is a human decision, so I left it proposed.\r\n\r\n[result] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=12 surface=295412075ba5\r\n"]
